    "Motor-to-cradle attachment is missing before cradle-to-chassis support can be designed. Actual vendor STEP cylindrical mounting lines run along canonical X at (y,z)=(7.5,-8) and (-22.5,-8), with radii0.8/1.0mm. These do not align with current generic plate holes along Z.",
    "Current motor and plate are separated by1.5mm. The plate is not a modeled motor bracket. M2 TAP8 identification/head seats are from retained V9 hardware code; the cylindrical STEP measurements independently establish the axes, not thread specification or tightening engagement.",
    "S101_relief is a reuse candidate, but inserting it at the current motor transform overlaps the generic plate by823.666147mm3. It requires a redesigned adapter/base, not simply another part added to the present assembly.",
    "The chassis floor has windows and load rails. An8mm-diameter nominal foot at many current plate-hole XY projections has no floor material; straight standoffs at all32 holes are not viable without a new supported footprint.",
    "Index PIP and ring DIP plates are elevated; their straight support columns may cross lower motors. Little PIP has its plate above the motor. These require lateral/bridged support or a newly validated bank orientation, not an assumed vertical post."
